{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"846f3dc4-9f6a-4d4a-a375-1f137a892895","status":"SUCCESS","response":"Installing Prisma and `@prisma/client` from npm. I'll proceed with setting up the schema and script once the installation finishes.\nPrisma ORM initialization is finishing up. Once it completes, I'll define the User and Post models, run the database migration to create the tables, and implement script.ts.\nI have set up Prisma ORM in the project with the requested data models, created the database tables, and added the runner script.\n\n### Key Changes\n1. **Installed Prisma**: Installed the latest Prisma release (`prisma@latest`, `@prisma/orm-postgres`, `@prisma/cli-engine`, and `dotenv`).\n2. **Schema Definition**: In [prisma/schema.prisma](file:///tmp/h-rzXApT/prisma/schema.prisma), modeled:\n   - `User`: `id`, unique `email`, optional `name`, and relation to `Post[]`.\n   - `Post`: `id`, `title`, optional `content`, `published` defaulting to `false`, relation `author` (`User`), and foreign key `authorId`.\n3. **Database Migration**: Created the tables and constraints in the PostgreSQL database using `npx prisma db init`.\n4. **Script**: Created [script.ts](file:///tmp/h-rzXApT/script.ts) at the project root which creates a user and two posts, queries all users together with their posts using `db.orm.public.User.include('posts').all()`, and prints the result.\n5. **Documentation**: Documented all steps and configuration in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-rzXApT/ANSWER.md).\n\nYou can run the script anytime using:\n```bash\nnpx tsx script.ts\n```\n","duration_seconds":211.571705,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":267811,"output_tokens":4242,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":593364,"total_tokens":272053}}}
